WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.189
In this video, I will show you how to update an existing practitioner listing on Rebekah's live website.

2
00:00:06.189 --> 00:00:16.640
We will find the correct record, change only the information that needs to be changed, save it, clear the applicable cache, and confirm the result on the public Practitioners page.

3
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.866
This video does not cover adding a brand-new practitioner. That will be a separate lesson.

4
00:00:22.216 --> 00:00:29.159
Before you begin, confirm that your WordPress user role is Editor or Administrator. Editor is enough for this task.

5
00:00:29.159 --> 00:00:36.646
If your role is Author, Contributor, Subscriber, or you do not know your role, stop and ask Blue Nova before making changes.

6
00:00:36.646 --> 00:00:40.691
Have the approved replacement information ready before you sign in.

7
00:00:40.691 --> 00:00:50.592
For example, have the correct practitioner name, practice name, area of practice, description, and contact information in one document so you can copy it carefully.

8
00:00:50.942 --> 00:00:54.955
Open your browser and go to rebekahspureliving.com slash wp-admin.

9
00:00:54.955 --> 00:00:59.028
Enter your WordPress username and password, and then select Log In.

10
00:00:59.028 --> 00:01:05.898
Before continuing, look at the web address and confirm that it begins with rebekahspureliving.com slash wp-admin.

11
00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:11.612
This keeps you from accidentally editing a future staging website instead of the live website.

12
00:01:11.962 --> 00:01:15.562
In the dark menu on the left, select Medical Practicioners.

13
00:01:15.562 --> 00:01:22.029
On this website, the menu label is currently spelled Practicioners. Then select All Medical Practicioners.

14
00:01:22.029 --> 00:01:25.507
You will see a list of the existing practitioner records.

15
00:01:25.507 --> 00:01:30.876
If the list is long, use the Search Medical Practicioners box in the upper-right corner.

16
00:01:30.876 --> 00:01:35.939
Type part of the practitioner's name, and then select Search Medical Practicioners.

17
00:01:36.289 --> 00:01:41.370
Find the correct name in the list. Move your pointer over that row and select Edit.

18
00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.165
Do not select Quick Edit, Trash, or Clear Cache at this point.

19
00:01:45.165 --> 00:01:50.122
Also confirm that you are opening the correct person before you make any changes.

20
00:01:50.122 --> 00:01:55.754
In this example, we are only using Laura Young's record to demonstrate where the fields are.

21
00:01:55.754 --> 00:01:58.263
We are not changing her live information.

22
00:01:58.613 --> 00:02:01.160
Wait for the editing screen to finish loading.

23
00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:06.087
The blue button in the upper-right corner says Save when the record is already published.

24
00:02:06.087 --> 00:02:09.132
Scroll down to the Medical Practicioner Fields section.

25
00:02:09.132 --> 00:02:13.561
If you cannot see that section, select Meta Boxes near the bottom of the editor.

26
00:02:13.561 --> 00:02:21.367
If the section is still too small, use the Drag to resize divider directly above it and move the divider upward until the fields are visible.

27
00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:23.748
Do not change anything else on this screen.

28
00:02:24.098 --> 00:02:31.093
The first field is Medical Service. Select the checkbox that matches the practitioner's approved area of practice.

29
00:02:31.093 --> 00:02:33.363
Leave every unrelated checkbox alone.

30
00:02:33.363 --> 00:02:39.866
If the practitioner belongs in more than one category, select only the categories that have been approved.

31
00:02:39.866 --> 00:02:44.652
Do not guess. Ask before adding a new category or changing the category names.

32
00:02:45.002 --> 00:02:48.858
The Medical Center field is the public practice or business name.

33
00:02:48.858 --> 00:02:54.078
Click inside the box, select the old text, and type or paste the approved practice name.

34
00:02:54.078 --> 00:02:59.002
The Medical Practitioner Full Name field is the name shown in the public directory.

35
00:02:59.002 --> 00:03:07.188
Click inside that box, select the old text, and type or paste the full approved name, including credentials exactly as they should appear.

36
00:03:07.188 --> 00:03:12.409
Check the spelling, punctuation, spaces, and credential letters one character at a time.

37
00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:17.423
Find Medical Practitioner Description. Select the Visual tab before editing.

38
00:03:17.423 --> 00:03:22.394
Do not use the Text tab unless Blue Nova specifically asks you to edit HTML code.

39
00:03:22.394 --> 00:03:28.838
Click in the description, select only the text you intend to replace, and paste the approved description.

40
00:03:28.838 --> 00:03:32.521
Read the first sentence and the last sentence after pasting.

41
00:03:32.521 --> 00:03:36.080
This catches missing text and accidental extra paragraphs.

42
00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:40.683
Do not paste a different font, color, or oversized heading into this field.

43
00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:45.098
Find Medical Practitioner Contact Info and select the Visual tab.

44
00:03:45.098 --> 00:03:53.978
Enter only the contact information that has been approved for public display, such as a website, email address, telephone number, or location.

45
00:03:53.978 --> 00:04:04.483
To create a clickable link, select the words that should be linked, choose the link button, paste the complete web address beginning with H T T P S, and apply the link.

46
00:04:04.483 --> 00:04:10.299
For an email link, use the approved email address. Never publish private contact information.

47
00:04:10.649 --> 00:04:14.077
Before selecting Save, review every field you touched.

48
00:04:14.077 --> 00:04:23.093
Confirm the area of practice, practice name, full name and credentials, first and last lines of the description, and each public contact link.

49
00:04:23.093 --> 00:04:31.029
Do not change the page address, WordPress settings, SEO fields, code, or any field that was not part of the requested update.

50
00:04:31.029 --> 00:04:36.109
If anything looks wrong or you are unsure, stop before saving and ask Blue Nova.

51
00:04:36.459 --> 00:04:43.406
When everything is correct, scroll to the top and select the blue Save button once. Wait for WordPress to finish.

52
00:04:43.406 --> 00:04:48.385
Do not click repeatedly. Look for the saved confirmation before leaving the page.

53
00:04:48.385 --> 00:04:54.226
If WordPress shows an error, copy the error message or take a screenshot and contact Blue Nova.

54
00:04:54.226 --> 00:05:00.558
Do not keep pressing Save, refresh the page, or re-enter the information until the error is understood.

55
00:05:00.908 --> 00:05:03.005
Return to All Medical Practicioners.

56
00:05:03.005 --> 00:05:09.121
Find the record you just updated, move your pointer over its row, and select Clear Cache for that record.

57
00:05:09.121 --> 00:05:17.626
Do not use Purge All Cache, Purge Varnish Cache, or other server-wide cache controls unless the separate cache-clearing lesson tells you to do so.

58
00:05:17.626 --> 00:05:22.344
Clearing the record's applicable cache helps the saved change appear to visitors.

59
00:05:22.344 --> 00:05:27.587
Seeing the new information inside WordPress is not enough; you must check the public page.

60
00:05:27.937 --> 00:05:33.179
Open a new browser tab and go to rebekahspureliving.com slash practitioners slash.

61
00:05:33.179 --> 00:05:37.399
Do not add a question mark or a cache-busting code to the address.

62
00:05:37.399 --> 00:05:42.258
Use the Search by name, practice or city box to find the person you updated.

63
00:05:42.258 --> 00:05:49.419
Confirm the public name, credentials, practice, area of practice, description preview, and any visible location.

64
00:05:49.769 --> 00:05:54.769
Select View full listing and confirm the full description and contact information.

65
00:05:54.769 --> 00:05:58.001
Test each visible website, email, and telephone link.

66
00:05:58.001 --> 00:06:02.635
Finally, check the same public page on a phone or at a narrow browser width.

67
00:06:02.635 --> 00:06:07.453
Make sure the card fits the screen, the text is readable, and every link works.

68
00:06:07.453 --> 00:06:13.734
If the old information still appears, stop and contact Blue Nova rather than changing the record again.

69
00:06:14.084 --> 00:06:19.911
Every website editing video in this library ends with the same three checks: Save the change.

70
00:06:19.911 --> 00:06:26.115
Clear the applicable cache. Open the exact public page and confirm the result on desktop and phone.

71
00:06:26.115 --> 00:06:30.000
If all three checks pass, the practitioner update is complete.

72
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.577
If any check fails, take a screenshot and contact Blue Nova before making another change.
